<h1>From Structure to Pattern Recognition</h1>

<div style="float: right; width: 35%; max-width: 270px; margin: 0 0 10px 20px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/a207931de42fa5f89ac47727c93b5143-image-1787596651446.png" alt="Four small website mockups in different color schemes, each following the same nav bar, hero section, gallery cards, and footer layout, with a magnifying glass highlighting the shared structure." style="width: 100%; border-radius: 10px;">
<p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 8px;"><b>Same structure, many sites</b></p>
</div>



<p>The site you just explored followed a familiar shape: nav bar, hero, gallery cards, footer. That's not a coincidence.</p>

<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• AI studied a huge number of real websites during training</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• It noticed that same structure repeat again and again</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Now it defaults to that shape automatically, even when a prompt never mentions it directly</p>

<br>

<p>AI doesn't read a prompt the way a person does, it predicts what a page like that usually looks like based on patterns it's seen before.</p>

<div style="clear: both;"></div>

<p><i>Below, try it yourself: generate a page from a prompt, then walk through what actually happened behind the scenes.</i></p>

---

